    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκυκλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-rounded, round</i>,
			in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> always of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπίς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				5.453
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				797
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				590
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. ἕδρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					4.66
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφαίρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					8.43
				</span></i>
